.TH ZERODDS-DURABILITY-SVC 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-durability-svc \- ZeroDDS Durability-Service daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-durability-svc
\fB\-\-domain\fR \fIN\fR
[\fB\-\-store\fR \fIsqlite\fR|\fIfile\fR|\fIlakehouse\fR|\fIpostgres\fR]
[\fB\-\-path\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-auto\fR]
[\fB\-\-topic\fR \fINAME\fR]...
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIYAML\fR]
[\fB\-\-set\fR \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR]...
.br
.B zerodds-durability-svc
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIYAML\fR]
[\fB\-\-set\fR \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR]...
\fB\-\-check\-config\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-durability-svc
keeps the samples of TRANSIENT and PERSISTENT topics (DDS 1.4 \(sc2.2.3.4)
for readers that join later, beyond the lifetime of the writers that
wrote them. One daemon serves one DDS domain; it discovers the topics
itself and replays their history to late joiners. PERSISTENT history
survives a restart of the daemon when the store is durable.
.PP
A discovered writer's own retention policy \(em its
.B DurabilityServiceQosPolicy
(DDS 1.4 \(sc2.2.3.5) \(em governs how long its topic's history is kept,
unless the configuration file pins a contract for that topic explicitly; see
.BR zerodds-durability-svc.yaml (5),
"WHICH CONTRACT WINS". A discovered topic's keyedness likewise comes from the
writer (its RTPS entityKind, DDSI-RTPS 2.5 \(sc9.3.1.2), not an assumption.
.SH OPTIONS
Every option below is
.B --set
of its configuration key (see
.BR zerodds-durability-svc.yaml (5)):
.BR \-\-domain\ N
is
.BR "--set domain=N" ,
.BR \-\-topic\ NAME
is
.BR "--set +durability.topics=NAME" ,
and so on \(em so the flag and an equivalent line in the file are the same
setting, and whichever applies last (files, then flags) wins. Per-topic
.BR type / keyed / contract
overrides have no flag: they are config-only (see
.BR zerodds-durability-svc.yaml (5)).
.TP
.BR \-\-domain " " \fIN\fR
The DDS domain id. Required (from this flag or the file).
.TP
.BR \-\-store " " \fIKIND\fR
The cold store:
.I sqlite
(default) or
.IR file ;
.I lakehouse
(DuckDB) and
.I postgres
only in a build with the features of the same name.
.TP
.BR \-\-path " " \fIPATH\fR
Where the store lives:
.IR sqlite / lakehouse ,
a database file (omitted: in memory, lost on restart);
.IR file ,
a directory (required);
.IR postgres ,
a libpq connection string (required).
.TP
.B \-\-auto
Serve every topic whose writers declare TRANSIENT or PERSISTENT
durability.
.TP
.BR \-\-topic " " \fINAME\fR
Serve this topic; repeatable. If the store already holds type/keyedness/
contract for it from an earlier run, it resumes immediately \(em no writer
or reader has to be discovered first. Otherwise its type and keyedness
resolve from whichever writer of it is discovered first (regardless of
durability kind, since the topic was named explicitly), unless the
configuration file names an explicit
.B type
for it. At least one of
.B \-\-auto
and
.B \-\-topic
is required (from any source, once every layer is merged).
.TP
.BR \-\-config " " \fIYAML\fR
The configuration file, with its drop-in directory
.IR YAML .d/;
default: the system configuration directory. Holds this daemon's own
settings (above) alongside the shared DDS runtime's.
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable;
.B --set\ +PATH=VALUE
appends to a list (e.g. another
.BR durability.topics " entry)."
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate and print the effective configuration \(em this daemon's own
settings and the shared DDS runtime's \(em with the origin of every value,
then exit (0 valid, 1 invalid value or unknown key, 2 unreadable file or
syntax error).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/zerodds-durability-svc.service
The unit; its environment
.RB ( ZERODDS_DURABILITY_DOMAIN ,
.BR ZERODDS_DURABILITY_STORE ,
.BR ZERODDS_DURABILITY_PATH ,
.BR ZERODDS_DURABILITY_EXTRA )
fills the command line. Default: domain 0, sqlite in
.IR /var/lib/zerodds/durability/dur.db ,
.BR \-\-auto .
.TP
.I /var/lib/zerodds/durability
The store directory of the unit, the only path it may write.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGTERM and SIGINT stop the daemon: the pumps are joined and it exits 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Stopped by a signal, or
.B \-\-check\-config
found the configuration valid.
.TP
.B 1
An invalid command line or configuration value, or the store could not be
opened.
.TP
.B 2
A configuration file could not be read or does not parse.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-durability-svc.yaml (5),
.BR zerodds-router (1),
.BR zerodds-admin (1)
.SH AUTHOR
ZeroDDS Contributors
